{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 1 — PROVEN root cause (rebar-debug)\n\n### Step 0 sweep\n- `Step 0(a): duplicates none.` The only near-match is `unreal-milky-sloth` /\n  `6fe7-956f-4901-45cf` (BigInt serialization), named in this ticket as candidate 2 — it is\n  CLOSED and is a different mechanism (see rejection below). No sibling to resume.\n- Reported-against floor: `created_at` 1787858559072112001 ns → main at/before 2026-08-25.\n  Behaviour reproduced on today's `origin/main` (afe01efaa8b2), so the floor is not material.\n\n### Discriminating experiment — the deployed endpoint, today\n\nUnfiltered `tools/call list_tickets {}` against `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp`\n(Streamable HTTP, bearer auth):\n\n    http=200  size=94541551  time=177.286450\n\n**The server did not fail.** It returned a well-formed JSON-RPC result of\n**94,541,551 bytes (94.5 MB) over 177 seconds**, in one SSE `event: message` frame.\n\nThat single observation separates all three candidate causes:\n\n1. **Response size — CONFIRMED.** 94.5 MB in one response, 177 s wall.\n2. **BigInt serialization — REJECTED.** The call completed and the payload parses; the\n   js-safe guard (`src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py:152` `js_safe_result`) is doing its job.\n3. **Deploy cutover — REJECTED.** Reproducible on demand three days after the 18:54:29Z\n   cutover, from a session that was never orphaned.\n\nSo the transport close is the **client** abandoning a 94.5 MB / 177 s single response, and it\nis client-dependent: Copilot CLI reports `Transport closed`; this Claude Code session's own\nconfig carries a 30 s connect budget (`claude mcp get rebar` → \"connection timed out after\n30000ms\"); a third client succeeded but had to spill 219,815 chars to disk. The server offers\nno bound and no structured signal, so none of them can distinguish \"too big\" from \"server died\".\n\n### The changeable artifact\n\n**The MCP read surface has exactly one payload bound and `list_tickets` is not wired to it.**\n\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:449-494` — `_WORKFLOW_TOKEN_BUDGET_BYTES = 90_000` and\n  `_cap_workflow_payload()`, whose own comment states the contract: *\"Keep MCP … payloads\n  under the client's ~25K-token budget (WS-ffc4).\"*\n- It is applied to **two** tools only: `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py:539` (`get_workflow_status`)\n  and `:553` (`get_workflow_result`).\n- `list_tickets` (`src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py:278-326`) returns\n  `[TicketStateOut.model_validate(t) for t in rebar.list_tickets(...)]` with **no size check\n  at all**. Same for `ready_tickets`, `search`, `next_batch`.\n\n### Why \"lean by default\" does not save it (question 3)\n\n`list_tickets`' docstring claims *\"lean by default — the bulky `description` and `comments`\nfields are omitted so a broad list stays small\"*. The claim is **literally true and materially\nfalse**. `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:494-496` is the whole lean path:\n\n    if not include_body:\n        ps.pop(\"description\", None)\n        ps.pop(\"comments\", None)\n\nMeasured against the real store (2,855 tickets), lean vs full is 44.4 MB vs 73.0 MB — a 39%\nsaving that leaves the actual bulk untouched. Aggregate field weights of the **lean** payload:\n\n| field | bytes | share of lean |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| `authorship_ledger` | 26,241,422 | 59% |\n| `attestations` | 10,370,251 | 23% |\n| `signature` | 2,639,114 | 6% |\n| everything else | 5,141,280 | 12% |\n\n**88% of the \"lean\" payload is base64 DSSE signature material** that a list caller never asked\nfor. Per row: 15,548 bytes lean; 1,726 bytes with those four fields (incl. `keyring`) dropped —\na 9x difference. The reported 10-row filtered call reproduces exactly: `tag=mcp, status=open,\ntype=bug` → 52,854 bytes lean, 11,178 bytes slim.\n\nThe mirror lean path in `src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_view.py:383` has the same two-field drop.\n\n### Legitimacy\n\nThis is a defect, not a misunderstanding: the behaviour diverges from two in-repo authoritative\nstatements — the `list_tickets` docstring's \"stays small\", and `_cap_workflow_payload`'s stated\n\"under the client's ~25K-token budget\" contract that the rest of the read surface ignores.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787946666352468402,"uuid":"2be0351e-8b9f-47c8-9c5f-d7e2753224ff"}